{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:00f9e9f4ca24e011","name":"CR70 Corellian Corvette","source":{"id":"source:reference-00f9e9f4ca24e011","title":"CR70 Corellian Corvette","revision":18680,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:32:41Z","sha256":"320a6f8e69668e1736f66394857119b6b16c744833315280e7fb77d7eff4a700","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18680","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=CR70%20Corellian%20Corvette&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-00f9e9f4ca24e011","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The predecessor to the more widely used ",{"tag":"a","children":["CR90 Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CR90_Corellian_Corvette","referenceId":"reference:b7c048e67aab87b7"},", the CR70 Corellian Corvette saw frequent use in diplomatic and transport roles. Unarmed and boasting additional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Escape Pods"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Escape_Pods"},", the CR70 was among the most popular civilian transports in the galaxy prior to the rise of the Empire. The CR70 Corvette had been in service for many years before the outbreak of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", and though it was considered an older design, it was still in production in large quantities during the years prior to the battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Geonosis"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Geonosis","referenceId":"reference:2f85e38b680a11c3"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The CR70 Corvette features an interior layout that is nearly identical to that of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["CR90 Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CR90_Corellian_Corvette","referenceId":"reference:b7c048e67aab87b7"},". The vessel has ",{"tag":"a","children":["Escape Pods"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Escape_Pods"}," where the CR90's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Turbolasers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Turbolasers"}," would be, disguised to look like ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," in order to deter pirates and raiders. Without the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Turbolaser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Turbolaser","referenceId":"reference:3f6c338dc202fcde"}," Batteries, some interior space dedicated to weapon support systems aboard the CR90 acts as cargo space or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Passenger Quarters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Passenger_Quarters"},", making space less of a premium aboard a CR70.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Vanguard c20 Retrofit"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When the Corellian Engineering Corporation began producing the ",{"tag":"a","children":["CR90 Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CR90_Corellian_Corvette","referenceId":"reference:b7c048e67aab87b7"}," as its standard (rather than as an upgrade), current owners of CR70 Corellian Corvettes were given the option of purchasing an aftermarket modification suite that brought the vessels up to date technologically with the CR90 Corvette. Known as the Vanguard c20 Retrofit, this modification enhanced the combat prowess of the Corellian Corvette and ensured that the CR70 remained on par with the CR90, essentially transforming the former into the latter. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Tantive IV"]},", for example, began as a CR70 Corellian Corvette that was used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bail Organa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bail_Organa","referenceId":"reference:25959f9d5a1655a3"}," at the tail end of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},". By the time of the Galactic Civil War, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Tantive IV"]}," had undergone retrofitting that transformed it into a ",{"tag":"a","children":["CR90 Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CR90_Corellian_Corvette","referenceId":"reference:b7c048e67aab87b7"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Vanguard c20 Retrofit costs 500,000 credits (which includes both raw materials as well as labor costs for having the retrofit applied) and usually takes 2 to 3 weeks of work by trained professionals. The process changes the base statistics for the CR70 Corellian Corvette to those of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["CR90 Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/CR90_Corellian_Corvette","referenceId":"reference:b7c048e67aab87b7"},", though this does not change the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crew Quality"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crew_Quality","referenceId":"reference:c79e9b6530a86284"}," by default.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["CR70 Corellian Corvette Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Frigate) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","ch